==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|re-|wind<id:turn coil>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈwaɪnd/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rewind.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|wind}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnd|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|~s|~ing|rewound}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[wind]] (something) [[again]].
#* {{RQ:Martin Storm of Swords|page=440|passage=A Myrish crossbowman poked his head out a different window, got off a bolt, and ducked down to '''rewind'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Paul Kelly|title=The Surgeon Was a Lady
|passage={{...}} she was winding and '''rewinding''' bandages that were dripping in blood, smiling strangely at her as the plasma spilled from buckets all over the floor.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[wind]] [[back]], of something [[clocklike]] or [[recordlike]], like a [[cassette]], [[tape]], [[film]]; especially to then [[replay]] or [[relive]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's '''rewind''' the clock to an earlier time.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Rewind''' the tape to the first chapter.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[regress]] the [[state]] of [[playback]] of a [[recording]].
#: {{ux|en|I've '''rewound''' the [[audiobook]] to the start of the chapter.}}
#: {{ux|en|This video player can '''rewind''' smoothly.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[go]] back or [[think back]] to a [[previous]] [[moment]] or [[place]], or a previous [[point]] in a [[discourse]].
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Ingrid Michaelson; w:Trent Dabbs; w:busbee|title=Time Machine|album={{w|Lights Out (Ingrid Michaelson album)|Lights Out}}|year=2014|artist=Ingrid Michaelson|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7GYm1pQyJA|text=If I had a time machine / And if life was a movie scene / I'd '''rewind''', and I'd tell me / "Ru-u-u-u-u-u-u-un"}}

